# New installations: use the one-command installer in README.md.
# For an existing HTTPS deployment, create/update this file with:
# python3 scripts/install_keep.py --url https://keep.example.com
# The command generates separate deployment secrets and restricts this file to
# the current user. Never commit the populated file.
# Optional: choose an image by immutable version tag or sha256 digest:
# KEEP_IMAGE=brspoon/keep:2.21.3
# KEEP_IMAGE=brspoon/keep@sha256:...
# New installs leave ownership unset; existing installs preserve their owner.
# PLEX_OWNER_ID=1234
# Configure services and email through Settings after the owner signs in.
# Optional override; otherwise Keep generates and persists a unique identifier.
# PLEX_CLIENT_IDENTIFIER=your-existing-identifier
# Advanced deployment settings (HTTPS and loopback are the defaults):
# KEEP_TRANSPORT_MODE=https
# KEEP_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# KEEP_PORT=5000
# Local HTTP requires explicit lan-http mode and a private IPv4 KEEP_URL.
# The installer sets all four values together for new LAN installations.
# Service overrides are optional advanced deployment settings; see docs/INSTALLATION.md.
